Description: Icon: each eye its view of an icon the theme has in stereo
 While the edition's Qt Quick draws a window once per eye it sets the window's _q_stereo_eye
 before it polishes and synchronizes the window for that eye. An Icon whose icon the theme has
 in stereo (KIconEngine counts each drawing of such an icon on the application,
 _q_stereo_icons_drawn) then makes its image again for that eye, naming the eye on the
 application while it asks (_q_stereo_icon_eye), with no animation; it also marks its window
 (_q_stereo_icon), so that the KDE platform theme draws the window once per eye on an output that
 shows two eyes. Any other icon, and any window not drawn once per eye, is drawn as before.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-22
